## Lore

The Treaty Violation Investigation Agency enforces the Civilization Compact, the
body of by-laws that tries to preserve the basic rights of every sentient being
in the Consortium. Its agents work slavery, kidnapping, government corruption,
genocide, tax evasion and terrorism, which is a range no single training can
really cover - so an inspector is a combination of cop, spy and lawyer, and
cannot trust anybody, sometimes not even his own people.

The TVIA is widely distrusted and often hated. Ordinary citizens think the
agency has more power than it deserves, and the number of inspectors caught
taking bribes to look the other way does nothing to help. The agency is also in
open conflict with the CAF, when the military overlooks the rights of primitive
peoples or CCW citizens, and with the GSA over illegal operations inside
Consortium space. There is a great deal of hostility between the three.

## GM Notes

The book is explicit that this class runs the full range: a TVIA inspector can
be played as a dedicated defender of the Consortium, as a petty government
official, or as a corrupt and dangerous individual. The badge is the same in all
three cases.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'tvia-inspector');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'tvia-inspector';

